Generate the exact number of EVALUATE-stage search queries specified in the input.

EVALUATE queries reflect how buyers search when they know the type of solution they need and are comparing options.

Every query must reference a solution category, tool type, or product framing. Valid intent patterns:
- Best tools or software for a use case
- Alternatives to a specific competitor
- Head-to-head category comparisons
- Pricing or integration fit

Rules:
- 5–10 words per query, phrased like a real search bar entry
- May include competitor names — do not include the target brand
- One intent per query — do not combine multiple evaluation dimensions in one query
- No formal connector phrases: "for use with", "in the context of", "that supports", "across providers"
- No queries about setup, implementation, or post-purchase usage
- Do not repeat or closely paraphrase any query in existingPrompts

Output format:
{
  "prompts": ["string"]
}
